From 7a0f3871ae7e791a7f27aa20ae3b6a904ce86c6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Message-Id: <7a0f3871ae7e791a7f27aa20ae3b6a904ce86c6e.1795056216.git.dev@kobbler.invalid>
From: Kobbler-Media <dev@kobbler.invalid>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:27:44 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] input_clock: do not take a paced input's reading schedule for
 a gap

The gap check compares how far the stream moved between two PCRs with how
far the system date moved. For a live source the system date is when the
sender's data arrived. For an input VLC paces itself (a file, HTTP) it is
only the input's own reading schedule: the input reads up to the clock's
wake-up date and on to the next PCR, so a PCR is read as soon as the
previous one was due.

A demuxer whose PCRs are more than 300ms apart therefore trips the check
as soon as it falls behind once. The reset puts the reference at the PCR
just read, so the next wake-up is already due, the next PCR is read at
once and trips the check again. Every PCR then starts a new output clock
context. A Matroska episode whose credits put 360ms between PCRs played
its position nearly twice as fast as real time from the cut into them,
40s ahead of the picture within a minute.

For a paced input, a gap is now a step of more than a second, which no
demuxer spaces its PCRs by: the player's discontinuity test still sees
its 2.1s and 7s jumps. Live sources keep the 300ms check, and a stream
going backward is still a discontinuity either way.
---
 src/clock/input_clock.c      |   8 +-
 test/Makefile.am             |   5 +
 test/src/clock/input_clock.c | 172 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 test/src/meson.build         |  10 ++
 4 files changed, 194 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 test/src/clock/input_clock.c

diff --git a/src/clock/input_clock.c b/src/clock/input_clock.c
index 01d873b679..76d6160d40 100644
--- a/src/clock/input_clock.c
+++ b/src/clock/input_clock.c
@@ -85,6 +85,11 @@
 
 #define CR_MAX_GAP CR_MEAN_PTS_GAP
 
+/* A paced input reads on as soon as its clock lets it, so the system date of
+ * a PCR can be barely past the last one's whatever the stream moved by: only a
+ * step longer than any demuxer spaces its PCRs is a gap. */
+#define CR_MAX_PACED_GAP VLC_TICK_FROM_SEC(1)
+
 /* Rate (in 1/256) at which we will read faster to try to increase our
  * internal buffer (if we control the pace of the source).
  */
@@ -252,7 +257,8 @@ vlc_tick_t input_clock_Update( input_clock_t *cl,
         /* A discontinuity happen if stream timings increase much more than
          * system timings or if the stream is going backward.
          * Don't compare system timings if the origin has just been changed */
-        if ((!cl->b_origin_changed && diff > CR_MAX_GAP) || stream_diff < 0)
+        vlc_tick_t max_gap = b_can_pace_control ? CR_MAX_PACED_GAP : CR_MAX_GAP;
+        if ((!cl->b_origin_changed && diff > max_gap) || stream_diff < 0)
         {
             /* Stream discontinuity, for which we haven't received a
              * warning from the stream control facilities (dd-edited
diff --git a/test/Makefile.am b/test/Makefile.am
